    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="8642d21b-ef49-5877-af8e-f84bd11505db" activityNameId="5d6ff61c-e696-5362-a77b-6212ff701a30" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Mineral filler, for asphalt concrete production, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Mineral filler, for asphalt concrete production, at plant
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 968fc20e-867c-4548-b48a-be016639b047
The filler was modelled based on the following composition: 57% quartz sand, 30% limestone, 7% feldspar, and 6% dolomite. The composition of the filler is based on a test report on the mineralogy of filler from Fabrique d’agglomérés Monthey SA and was taken from the research project ‘Life Cycle Assessment of Asphalt Pavements’ of the platform ‘Gravel for Generations’. For the milling process of dolomite, quartz sand, and feldspar, the same effort as for limestone was assumed.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: Production of 1 kg of mineral filler from the materials silica sand, limestone, feldspar, and dolomite, using a milling process to achieve the required particle size.
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_968fc20e-867c-4548-b48a-be016639b047.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
